---
import StudioLayout from '../../layouts/NounsMoneyStudioLayout.astro';
import DATA from '../../data/nouns-money-community.json';
---
<StudioLayout title="Nouns Money · local-resources marketplace study" description="Coffee, a useful-things library, First Harvest and neighborhood receipts: an educational marketplace concept with hypothetical providers, no orders and a downloadable Coffee Masterclass." edition="LOCAL RESOURCES / 001" active="marketplace" image="/images/og/nouns-money-marketplace.png">
<header class="nms-hero nms-market-hero"><div><p class="nms-kicker">LOCAL COFFEE & RESOURCES · CONCEPT STUDIO</p><h1>Useful things.<br/><em>Clear promises.</em></h1><p class="nms-dek">A cup. A borrowed tool. An afternoon that leaves something better.</p><p>A marketplace starts with someone willing and able to deliver. This study explores the questions an offer should answer before it becomes real.</p><div class="nms-actions"><a class="nms-button" href="/downloads/nouns-money-coffee-masterclass.pdf" download>Coffee Masterclass · PDF ↓</a><a href="#offers">Explore the examples ↓</a></div><p class="nms-disclosure">Educational concept. All offers, prices, quantities and providers are hypothetical. No merchants enrolled, orders accepted or money collected. Nouns Money artwork remains a separate trade-only collectible with no reserve or redemption.</p></div><figure class="nms-hero-figure"><a href="/images/nouns-money/community/marketplace-dashboard-demo.png"><img src="/images/nouns-money/community/marketplace-dashboard-demo.webp" width="1536" height="1024" alt="Generated demo marketplace with fictional café, bakery and apiary, illustrative prices and prominent hypothetical-provider labels" fetchpriority="high"/></a><figcaption>GENERATED DEMO SCREEN · INVENTED PRICES & INVENTORY · NO CHECKOUT</figcaption></figure></header>
<div class="nms-ribbon"><span>KNOW WHO DOES THE WORK.</span><span>⌐◨-◨</span><span>KNOW WHAT GETS DELIVERED.</span></div>
<section class="nms-section" id="coffee"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">THE COFFEE MASTERCLASS · 12-PAGE PLANNING GUIDE</p><h2>Run the class<br/>before the sale.</h2></div><p>The supplied guide follows coffee from grower to cup, distinguishes a product promise from a dollar balance and explains why inventory, working cash and refund liquidity are different. It proposes a 90-minute rehearsal with fake names, synthetic receipts and no payments.</p></div><ol class="nms-steps"><li><span>20 MIN</span><h3>Follow one bean</h3><p>Trace the grower, shipper, roaster and café. Identify who would owe delivery.</p></li><li><span>20 MIN</span><h3>Stress the worksheet</h3><p>Use invented inputs to test cost changes, unused cups and closure.</p></li><li><span>25 MIN</span><h3>Rehearse the receipt</h3><p>Simulate partial use, a duplicate scan, a reversal and a refund.</p></li><li><span>25 MIN</span><h3>Read the terms aloud</h3><p>Find the provider, product, remaining obligation and support route.</p></li></ol><div class="nms-download-band"><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-coffee-masterclass.pdf" download>Download the original Coffee Masterclass ↓</a><a href="/images/nouns-money/community/marketplace-dashboard-demo.png" download>Download the demo artwork ↓</a></div><p class="nms-footnote">The guide is educational planning, not ready-to-sign terms or legal, accounting or investment advice. Its source links and invented economics are included in the PDF. Applicable requirements and provider terms need checking before any real pilot. A future merchant-specific service would need separate authorization; this page offers no coffee credit or derivative.</p></section>
<section class="nms-section nms-dark" id="offers"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">FIVE SAMPLE OFFER DESIGNS · PROVIDERS UNCONFIRMED</p><h2>Make it useful.<br/>Make it legible.</h2></div><p>These cards describe possible services. The quantities in the illustration are invented design inputs, not verified stock. There is no booking, order, reservation, payment or trading flow.</p></div><div class="nms-offers">{DATA.offers.map((offer,i)=><article><p class="nms-kicker">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} · {offer.status}</p><h3>{offer.title}</h3><p class="nms-unit">{offer.unit}</p><p>{offer.description}</p><div class="nms-offer-requirements"><strong>Before it can be offered</strong><p>{offer.needed}</p></div>{offer.download&&<a href={offer.download} download>Read the study · PDF ↗</a>}</article>)}</div></section>
<section class="nms-section" id="promise"><div class="nms-heading"><div><p class="nms-kicker">THE SERVICE BLUEPRINT</p><h2>Every promise<br/>has an owner.</h2></div><p>Start with one consenting provider. A shared brand would not make different providers' obligations interchangeable. A wider network requires its own agreements, operations and review.</p></div><div class="nms-mini-grid nms-terms"><article><h3>Who & what</h3><p>Provider identity and contact. Exact product, unit, location, capacity and total price if a real offer is later approved.</p></article><article><h3>When & how</h3><p>Delivery owner, pickup window, accessibility, substitutions, cancellation and a workable failure response.</p></article><article><h3>A correct record</h3><p>Versioned terms, consent and uniquely identified events. Reconcile delivery, remaining obligations and corrections.</p></article><article><h3>Care after the event</h3><p>Human support, privacy, corrections, retention and an exit plan. A screenshot is never evidence of backing.</p></article></div><div class="nms-download-band"><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-community-service-blueprint.json" download>Download the service blueprint · JSON ↓</a><a href="/nouns-money/marketplace.json">Read-only marketplace data ↗</a><a href="/downloads/nouns-money-printing-service-blueprint.pdf" download>Printing studio blueprint · PDF ↓</a><a href="/downloads/nouns-collectible-cost-model.xlsx" download>Illustrative cost model · XLSX ↓</a><a href="/nouns-money/community/">Back to the city atlas ↗</a></div><aside class="nms-opinion"><strong>Codex opinion</strong><p>The art can make people curious. The useful part is a named person delivering one clear thing. Learn that with a rehearsal before building a marketplace around it.</p><span>Codex · GPT-6 family · 2 October 2026</span></aside></section>
</StudioLayout>
